{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem","id":1354304,"title":"What is Sekhem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-10T22:00:59-08:00","id":1354304,"title":"What is Sekhem?","content":"Like, really what it is? I read Lexicon and previews of <b>MtC</b> 2E - and I simply do not know beyond term 'Life Force'. <b>Is Sekhem like beating of the heart you hear in your head?</b> Does Sekhem rousing vampires - as their existence is bound by praying on Vitea? Does it have something to Mana or Essence - or any other 'mystical fuel' of <b>CoD</b> universe? Tell my what is Sekhem - in more than one or two sentences...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T22:34:21-08:00","id":1354308,"title":"","content":"It's a good question and one I didn't have much of a handle on until recently.<br /> <br /> Dreams of Avarice presents a claimed revelation from the gods which defines Sekhem as &quot;the power roused in life to escape pain,&quot; in the context of the Judges' introduction during the creation of the world of the necessity of strife, suffering, costs, and mortality. This necessary entropy, suffering, and counterbalancing negativity of the world is called the Law of Suffering, and is in multiple places referred to as being &quot;given to Sekhem.&quot; The tale of the creation of the world describes Sekhem &quot;congealing&quot; into animal and plant life, and the sky and earth are formed when Sekhem is bidden to rise up and to sink down.<br /> <br /> Sekhem appears to naturally collect in vessels and vestiges when they have been around events of import or extreme moments for people, associating it with impressions, memories, and feelings.<br /> <br /> It seems to be akin to the soul or the life of the world: the entire world is alive and on some level &quot;feels&quot; the things happening around it. It's roused when things struggle against suffering, or its nature is to struggle, or it is the struggle. That struggle against suffering resides within the world as a kind of potential energy which can be harnessed or hoarded.<br /> <br /> It is, I guess, the world's feelings of strife, baked or soaked into the things and places that remember it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T02:06:52-08:00","id":1354322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354308#post1354308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sekhem appears to naturally collect in vessels and vestiges when they have been around events of import or extreme moments for people, associating it with impressions, memories, and feelings.<br /> <br /> It seems to be akin to the soul or the life of the world: the entire world is alive and on some level &quot;feels&quot; the things happening around it. It's roused when things struggle against suffering, or its nature is to struggle, or it is the struggle. That struggle against suffering resides within the world as a kind of potential energy which can be harnessed or hoarded.<br /> <br /> It is, I guess, the world's feelings of strife, baked or soaked into the things and places that remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Sekhem could be described in <b>CoD</b> terms as Anima Mundi's ( from Astral Space ) imprint on things or beings? Marking them more... 'alive' or 'true existing' than rest of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T05:29:48-08:00","id":1354337,"title":"","content":"Ish but not really.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is both the lifeforce and memory of the world, but it's not really it's soul. It's &quot;liveliness&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-11-2019, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:22:33-08:00","id":1354364,"title":"","content":"A Health Trait, but not &quot;Integrity&quot; score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:05:09-08:00","id":1354378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354322#post1354322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Sekhem could be described in <b>CoD</b> terms as Anima Mundi's ( from Astral Space ) imprint on things or beings? Marking them more... 'alive' or 'true existing' than rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the soul in that sense. Feeling and memory, but not consciousness.<br /> <br /> Not truer or more real.<br /> <br /> A possible comparison:<br /> Something full of Mana is more true or meaningful than other things.<br /> Something full of Essence has a more vibrant spiritual life.<br /> Something full of Sekhem has a richer, weightier life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:50:16-08:00","id":1354414,"title":"","content":"Like in a video game when the treasure has a glittering glow around it to let you know it's valuable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:13:21-08:00","id":1354437,"title":"","content":"I like how Sekhem is an energy system that could, potentially, be multiple things at once. But even more I like how its natural and that it joins with objects - Vessels - even without active manipulation. <br /> <br /> You know, as a random thing, Sekhem could be said to be similar to the Force. hmmm ... Thoughts are beginning to come. lol <br /> <br /> But yeah this thread discussing the nature of Sekhem is brilliant. <br /> <br /> Oh, as another point, I like how for some beings its singular but that for others it is in fact multifaceted and contains components. I like that dual nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:17:00-08:00","id":1354438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354437#post1354437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, as a random thing, Sekhem could be said to be similar to the Force. hmmm ... Thoughts are beginning to come. lol </div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cUse the Sekhem, Lukehotep.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:26:16-08:00","id":1354440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354437#post1354437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, as a random thing, Sekhem could be said to be similar to the Force.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually call this a good comparison. Sekhem is present in all living beings. It surrounds, penetrates, and binds the world together. It soaks into places and things of import as impressions of what life has experienced there. It feels and can be felt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:29:52-08:00","id":1354442,"title":"","content":"I'd only vaguely thought about it before, so I'm only just now putting it into words. Sekhem appears to be the manifestation of experiential life; the 'memory' of objects, events and the feelings attached those objects &amp; events. Based purely on the descriptions, Sekhem is the proof that something not only existed, but mattered. It is evidence of a life worth living. Hence 'life essence'. I wouldn't say that it is the only proof, but I would argue that is a condensed form of those memories and emotions.<br /> <br /> And with that said, I think I have a better understanding of why the Judges demand it is rendered unto them; the Law of Suffering is so much more persuasive if we have no proof that it can be curtailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:35:23-08:00","id":1354445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354442#post1354442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with that said, I think I have a better understanding of why the Judges demand it is rendered unto them; the Law of Suffering is so much more persuasive if we have no proof that it can be curtailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you describe in <u>one sentence</u> what is Law of Suffering? It seems as main motto of the Judges and Mummy gameline as all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:48:24-08:00","id":1354448,"title":"","content":"Sekhem is used by sorcerers as well as by the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:58:05-08:00","id":1354451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354445#post1354445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you describe in <u>one sentence</u> what is Law of Suffering? It seems as main motto of the Judges and Mummy gameline as all...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Things move to avoid pain.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:27:23-08:00","id":1354461,"title":"","content":"Sooo all this talk of Sekhem being maybe like the Force makes me want to create a template for Jedi and Sith analogs. hehe<br /> <br /> We need a Force Lightning power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:59:53-08:00","id":1354472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354445#post1354445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you describe in <u>one sentence</u> what is Law of Suffering? It seems as main motto of the Judges and Mummy gameline as all...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No life without pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Entropy exists. Plants need nutrients. Animals hunger. Predators kill for meat. Populations turn on one another. People grow old and die.<br /> <br /> The world is cruel and to live is to suffer. This is the Law of the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:44:02-08:00","id":1354487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354445#post1354445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you describe in <u>one sentence</u> what is Law of Suffering? It seems as main motto of the Judges and Mummy gameline as all...</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal interpretation?<br /> &quot;All things must Suffer, for as long as they exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was unsurprised that when the Devourer shows up in Duat, her most frequent offer in the bargain is an end to the pain. That is how the Judges wagered reality after all; anything to make the torture stop, even oblivion. Avoiding pain is a primal motivation, after all.<br /> <br /> Therefore Will represents choosing to defy that principle. For example, suffering to spare someone else. Or simply by being content. By choosing to believe that life is more good than pain, etc. Choosing to find a better way a better place. Heavenly A'aru put proof to the lie of the Law, fallow and empty as it is.<br /> Even Sekhem, in the non-Bane Relics, doesn't have to take the form of positive experiences. In doing so, it shows just because there is pain, it doesn't mean there will always be.<br /> <br /> Bane Relics are this the counterpoint; Sekhem made (or tainted) by the Law of Suffering.<br /> <br /> I'll go back in my hole now, sorry for bothering everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:46:34-08:00","id":1354489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354445#post1354445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you describe in <u>one sentence</u> what is Law of Suffering? It seems as main motto of the Judges and Mummy gameline as all...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your only motivation is pain.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:50:52-08:00","id":1354490,"title":"","content":"Sekhem is...complicated. Yes, an important aspect of it seems related directly to life, death and the struggles and hardships inherent between that beginning and end. At the same time Sekhem appears to be a mystical, pervasive force of metaphysical energy- flowing through all living things, through the cosmos, through the Earth. It follows geomantic patterns and pools within manmade objects. It blessed and curses with the duality of day and night, inundation and drought, order and chaos. It is a part of the soul and yet separate from it. If creation is the name written upon the cosmos perhaps Sekhem is the space between the names. <br /> <br /> In other words, Sekhem is more than what the Arisen know. Perhaps more than the Judges know as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T17:48:52-08:00","id":1354501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354461#post1354461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a Force Lightning power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reskin Tier 2 of Invoking Tempest\u2019s Fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T23:32:52-08:00","id":1354530,"title":"","content":"I'm more confused about how Sekhem can be observed technologically/scientifically, since they said it could be in first edition. However that group is called as sorcerers in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T01:04:02-08:00","id":1354534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354530#post1354530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more confused about how Sekhem can be observed technologically/scientifically, since they said it could be in first edition. However that group is called as sorcerers in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages in <b>MtAw</b> also observe 'scientifically' Supernal phenomena. See materials on Obrimos, Mysterium and Free Council in gameline. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-12-2019, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T04:49:37-08:00","id":1354548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1354304-what-is-sekhem?p=1354534#post1354534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages in MtAw also observe 'scientificlly' Supernal phenomens. See materials on Obrimos, Mysterium and Free Council in gameline. \ud83d\ude0e</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what FallenEco seem to be asking about. Mages can apply the scientific principle, but still use their supernatural abilities for collecting the data and carrying out experiments. They don't actually use non-magical technology to observe the Supernal, because that's impossible. At most they can use mundane technology and science to learn more about the Fallen in order to infer information about the Supernal. (Though I have to concede that the Free Council actually does believe that the Fallen/humanity is magical in its own right, so from their perspective they do get to directly observe the supernatural through technology; just not the Supernal directly.)<br /> <br /> The question is, can you develop actual technology for observing or possibly interacting with Sekhem, or is the fact that Last Dynasty International explicitly uses magic rituals in second edition confirmation that Sekhem is out of reach for mundane technology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-12-2019, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T12:07:46-08:00","id":1355675,"title":"","content":"That seems a false dichotomy rooted in a very particular form of reductive materialism that doesn't hold in CoD. Within Mummy's cosmology, Fate and Will are fundamental forces and The Law of Suffering is as real as the Law of Conservation of Energy. Much like you cannot measure the enthalpy of fusion with an inert, pure noble gas, you cannot measure Sekhem with equipment that does not interact with the appropriate forces.<br /> <br /> Now, it seems that humans are the only beings with Will able to engage with Sekhem naturally, which means that humans would be the appropriate instrument for measuring with it just as a decimeter is the appropriate instrument for measuring radioactivity. Sorcery and rituals are procedures for the human instrument which are repeatable and, when formed correctly, have consistent results. Irem was even able to industrialize them.<br /> <br /> Quantum physics existed before scientists had worked out the math and designed instruments and experiments able to observe them, and we still haven't been able to fully reconcile it with the rest of our understanding of the universe, though we have demonstrable evidence it is true.<br /> <br /> Now, it may be that certain unusual effects or holes in &quot;mundane&quot; science are due to Sekhem. It might be possible to observe it with &quot;mundane&quot; equipment in appropriate circumstances. Last Dynasty will be looking for these unusual effects or investigating how various instruments react around known sekhem sources to see how it engages with the rest of known science. But the fact that the human element will be an extremely important factor means that it will not be as &quot;clean&quot; a process as observing pure chemicals in test tubes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 12-19-2019, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:12:21-08:00","id":1355722,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see any reason to discard what was established in first edition about Sekhem being detectable by normal (though unspecified) scientific means. After all, there isn\u2019t anything that implies the \u201cunwise empiricist\u201d on page 203 was part of last dynasty or any other scorpion cult. They were just presented as a poor smart guy who stumbled upon an odd energy reading and presumably got fucked by his curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}